// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-045
=adr: 045
=title: user-based-dashboard-sharing
=date: 2026-03-10
=status: accepted

#ctx
~problem: Public shareToken links bypass auth — any URL holder sees the dashboard.
~requirement: Share dashboards with specific org Viewer accounts; login required.
~current: Dashboard model has shareToken+shareEnabled (public, no-auth access).

#opts
~opt1: Keep public link + add user whitelist (sharedWithUsers[]) alongside it
~opt2: Replace public link entirely with sharedWithUsers[] — auth-only access [CHOSEN]

#decision
=remove: shareToken, shareEnabled fields from Dashboard model + all /share/:token routes
=add: sharedWithUsers: ObjectId[] on Dashboard (ref User)
=index: { sharedWithUsers: 1 }
=new_routes:
  POST /dashboards/:id/share  body:{userIds[]}  perm:dashboard:share  (Admin/Operator)
  GET  /dashboards/my         requireAuth       returns viewer-assigned dashboards
=viewer_ux: after login role==Viewer → redirect /viewer (kiosk, no sidebar/topbar)
=multi_dash: viewer sees tab strip if multiple dashboards assigned
=rbac: dashboard:read, dashboard:write, dashboard:share, dashboard:delete added to PERMISSIONS

#consequences
~all existing /view/:shareToken URLs break (page deleted)
~useSharedDeviceState hook deleted (was public-only)
~getDashboard service gates on sharedWithUsers for Viewer role
~KosmosShell share button opens ShareUsersModal instead of copying link
~root layout hides Sidebar+TopBar for role==Viewer
~login redirects Viewer to /viewer instead of /

#scope
=arch_summary_update: yes
